cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AtomInterface in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "AtomInterface: reliable interface modeling for atomistic materials simulations"
version: 0.6.0
date-released: 2026-11-03
authors:
  - name: "Feng Qi"
    affiliation: "Guangdong Zixiang Technology Co., Ltd."
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/aaminute-hash/atominterface"
url: "https://github.com/aaminute-hash/atominterface"
keywords:
  - materials science
  - interfaces
  - machine learning
  - atomistic simulation
  - density functional theory
  - molecular dynamics
abstract: >-
  AtomInterface is a Python middleware for building and evaluating atomistic
  models of interfaces between two crystalline materials. It wraps ASE,
  pymatgen, MACE and CHGNet and adds a reliability layer: coherent interface
  enumeration, an always-on relaxation guard against out-of-distribution and
  non-physical states, fail-closed interface-energy assembly, and a bridge that
  normalizes the output of thirteen simulation codes to one physical convention.
